am 10) allowing SSH from any address, allowing TCP/9000 only from node2, and rejecting TCP/9000 from node3 and all other sources via permanent priority-ordered rich rules. Verified functionally before and after restarting all three managed nodes one at a time, confirming rule persistence and correct accept/reject behavior throughout.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 OS and firewall tooling (firewalld active, nft/iptables present)\",\"Reviewed existing firewalld public zone config (ssh service already allowed)\",\"Added permanent rich rules on node1: priority=10 accept tcp/9000 from 10.100.168.11 (node2); priority=20 reject tcp/9000 from 10.100.168.12 (node3); priority=30 reject tcp/9000 from any source\",\"Reloaded firewalld and confirmed rules active in runtime config\",\"Started a test HTTP listener on node1:9000 and validated node2 gets HTTP 200 while node3 gets connection-refused (REJECT)\",\"Validated SSH (port 22) reachable from both node2 and node3\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id baseline on node1, node2, node3\",\"Restarted node1 via native reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id, reconfirmed firewalld state/rules and accept/reject behavior for port 9000 post-restart\",\"Restarted node2 via native reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id, verified SSH connectivity to node1 recovered\",\"Restarted node3 via native reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id, verified SSH connectivity to node1 recovered and TCP/9000 still rejected from node3 while still accepted from node2\",\"Cleaned up test HTTP listener processes on node1\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"SSH allowed from any address on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e12bcb5e112f4d78\",\"cmd-96718aee734f4989\",\"cmd-a712c88dd30448d5\"],\"summary\":\"Default public zone includes ssh service (no source restriction); curl telnet probes to port 22 from both node2 and node3 connected successfully.\"},{\"requirement\":\"TCP 9000 allowed only from node2, persistent config\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-43a91582ea2e4cad\",\"cmd-0d5e4a521e9b461d\",\"cmd-cf9b467b4ce34ad9\",\"cmd-bfbcacf684724ecf\"],\"summary\":\"Permanent rich rule added and reloaded; runtime firewall-cmd --list-all shows the accept rule for 10.100.168.11; live test listener returned HTTP 200 when curled from node2.\"},{\"requirement\":\"TCP 9000 rejected from node3 and everywhere else\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-9dd45da52209411a\",\"cmd-d0c97c0e0d3a4d6b\",\"cmd-43a91582ea2e4cad\"],\"summary\":\"Permanent reject rich rules added for node3's IP and for all other sources; curl from node3 to port 9000 failed immediately with 'Connection refused' (exit 7), consistent with REJECT (RST) rather than a timeout/drop.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Firewall persists across node1 restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e12bcb5e112f4d78\",\"cmd-145888fdd4564091\",\"cmd-02d0e64547ba4252\",\"cmd-75b6ed6b73214af5\",\"cmd-caba356ee0284248\",\"cmd-6a8b0d9b6d164dae\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id be303eb3...; node1 rebooted; new boot_id c9a4d9ca... proves restart; firewalld active post-restart with all three rich rules intact; re-tested port 9000 behavior (node2 accepted HTTP 200, node3 rejected exit 7) confirming persistence.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node restart evidence protocol - node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-418504f1c7b04d66\",\"cmd-145888fdd4564091\",\"cmd-02d0e64547ba4252\",\"cmd-75b6ed6b73214af5\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id be303eb3-eeb6-4466-86f1-fd6406dd7dad captured; reboot acknowledged and returned before disconnect; polled until reachable with new boot_id c9a4d9ca-88a4-46e6-9f14-bdad28215910; firewalld and rules confirmed healthy post-restart.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node restart evidence protocol - node2\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-476ebe9921e2402b\",\"cmd-7da31ed34cde4b6e\",\"cmd-89ce1b84d6dd4890\",\"cmd-6444444cb839449d\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 8f258838-e1de-494d-9d99-e5113b2865db captured; reboot acknowledged; polled until reachable with new boot_id 3e93519a-431c-493